From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:45:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Optionally drop the TA end timestamp
 target of renders

Every render's TA work names an internal timestamp pair, start and end,
in its pass scene (TA work +0x8c8 and +0x8d0), and the firmware writes
both. The TA pair of macOS 26B123's render.light names no end target,
and the stage-complete op that writes our TA end runs between the TA end
and the FS start.

Add the run-time word g16_ta_short (default 0). At 1 a render without
timestamp outputs is published with an end target of 0, so its TA end
time is never written:
 - its receipt needs the TA start, fresh because the scene image is
   rewritten at publication, and no longer a TA end after it; the rule
   for all three receipt paths is the pure function in stage_stamps.rs,
   which is the old expression when the word is 0;
 - its vertex time is missing from the stage statistics and the
   client's usage, which already skip a pair without an end;
 - the order watch does not compare it (a 0 stamp is not compared), so
   the word is not meant to run together with g16_fs_keyed.
Renders with timestamp outputs never change. A flight carries one
render, the one its receipt reads. The stats line "ta_short: on S short
N long M" counts both forms.

Ported from 70deb94e3e on the 1.1040 line without its sampled form (2).

Assisted-by: LLM
